sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant R as Flask route + generator
    participant Q as queue.Queue
    participant G as LangGraph daemon thread

    B->>R: POST /api/query {query, provider, model?}
    Note over B,R: fetch + ReadableStream, NOT<br/>EventSource — the query is a<br/>POST that carries a body
    Note over B,R: 400 on a blank query or an<br/>unknown provider — the only<br/>HTTP error status in the run
    R->>Q: create_session(uuid4())
    R->>G: Thread(target=_run, daemon=True).start()
    Note over Q,G: the hand-off — a disconnect frees<br/>the SOCKET, never the COMPUTE
    R-->>B: 200 text/event-stream
    Note over B,R: headers committed → every later<br/>failure is an in-band error<br/>delivered on a 200

    G->>G: node 1 · planner
    G->>Q: stage "planner" — retrieve? use_external? query_type
    Q->>R: q.get(timeout=180)
    R-->>B: data: {json}
    Note over B,R: shown once — the generator drains<br/>continuously, in strict FIFO order.<br/>180 s is PER EVENT, so the clock<br/>resets on every frame

    alt _route_planner — retrieve is true: the default path, enter the graph at retrieval
        G->>G: enter at node 2 · retrieval
        Note over Q,G: every node runs — 2 through 8
    else retrieve false but use_external true: skip the corpus, answer from the web
        G->>G: enter at node 3 · external_tools
        Note over Q,G: node 2 is skipped — the corpus<br/>is never searched
    else neither: answer straight from the model, gathering no evidence at all
        G->>G: enter at node 4 · aggregate
        Note over Q,G: nodes 2 and 3 skipped — no<br/>evidence is gathered at all
    end

    Note over B,G: The 5 emits marked * carry a stage id that DIFFERS from the graph node name.<br/>The emit() call site is the contract, never workflow.py — change an emitted id and the<br/>frontend tracker silently stops updating that row.

    loop retry — max 2, so 3 passes
        G->>G: node 2 · retrieval
        G->>Q: stage "retrieval" — vector 10 · BM25 10 · graph 5, in series
        G->>G: node 3 · external_tools
        G->>Q: stage "external_tools" — DuckDuckGo 5, or stage_skip
        G->>G: node 4 · aggregate
        G->>Q: * stage "aggregator" — dedup by MD5 of content
        G->>G: node 5 · rerank
        G->>Q: * stage "reranker" — cross-encoder, top 5
        G->>G: node 6 · compress
        G->>Q: * stage "compressor" — skipped below 4000 chars
        G->>G: node 7 · reason
        G->>Q: * stage "reasoning" — cited answer
        G->>G: node 8 · reflect
        G->>Q: * stage "reflection" — critic AND terminator
        Note over Q,G: retry iff NOT grounded AND should_retry<br/>AND retry_count < 2 — it emits retry,<br/>then re-enters the graph at node 2.<br/>_route_reflection tests final_answer<br/>alone, nothing else
    end

    G->>Q: done {answer, sources, metadata} — bypasses emit()
    G->>Q: finally: put(None) — the sentinel
    R-->>B: data: stream_end
    R->>Q: close_session() — pops the queue
    Note over B,G: done · error · stream_end are ROUTE-framed, not node-emitted. No node writes them,<br/>and a pipeline failure is a 200 carrying an error event, never an HTTP error status.
